{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>When a person sins.</b> Rabbi Akiva said: what does Scripture mean by ״ומעלה מעל בה״ — that he commits a breach of trust against it? Because everyone who borrows or lends, or who extends credit or gives, does so only with witnesses and a deed. Therefore when he denies, he denies the witnesses and the deed. But one who deposits with his fellow does not want any soul to know except a third party between them. Therefore when he denies, he denies the third party between them (there)." "<b>In trust.</b> That he placed money in his hand to do business with, or as a loan." "<b>Or by robbery.</b> That he robbed something from his hand." "<b>Or by oppression.</b> That is the wage of a hired laborer (there)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:06.926376277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}